  "intermediateFailures": [
    "Native capture established that Codex rejects CLI permission overrides for remote resume. The revised launch does not submit a permission override; the relay independently supplies and verifies the reviewed restrictions.",
    "An intermediate diagnostic attempted to echo a close frame after the native peer had already closed its write side. Its BrokenPipe failure and verified child cleanup remain retained.",
    "The first production bootstrap diagnostic closed the test socket before terminating the terminal, causing a teardown-only reconnect display. The corrected check retires the terminal first and verifies no reconnect; the transcript check repeats that ordering.",
    "The 13-group integration run predates one additional test-only malformed-bootstrap/account-change case and five more optional-method assertions. The final focused run covers those additions with 27 passing tests; implementation is unchanged."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This demonstration uses the native terminal with a synthetic provider and legacy saved transcript. It is not authenticated live-provider or actual VS Code GUI acceptance.",
    "Paginated native history is not implemented in this resume dialect; initialTurnsPage must still be null. Other native TUI versions need their own reviewed contract.",
    "The native terminal displays two skills-unavailable messages because optional feature reads are explicitly refused; no empty-success response is fabricated.",
    "The installed app remains ec28d09 and installed VS Code commands remain source 99784a7 until a normal verified update.",
    "No physical keyboard, installed account, real saved task, model request or user configuration was touched. The isolated CLI receives update/analytics/feedback-disabled settings only for the diagnostic."
  ]
